      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142313",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a sample of size $n = 64$ from a population. Given that the sample mean is $60$, and the sample standard deviation is $24$, find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\u03bc$ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T > 2.656) = 0.005$, where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $63$ degrees of freedom.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
